# RDE Agent Guardrails

Read `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, and
`docs/engineering/agent-correction-playbook.md` before changing code.

- **Session start:** read and follow
  `.claude/skills/dev-machine-profile/SKILL.md` — run
  `.venv/bin/python3 -m rde machine-profile --json` before any backend/GPU claim.
- Run project code only with `.venv/bin/python3`; never debug dependency
  failures with system Python.
- **Before backend or GPU claims**, use the detected `profile_id` from
  `machine-profile`; do not assume Intel vs Apple Silicon from prose.
- **New hot paths must be optimization-first** (MLX/vectorization/batching/workers
  from the first commit). See `.cursor/rules/optimization-first-architecture.mdc`.
- **Before writing any RDE experiment**, follow
  `src/rde/docs/experiment-playbook.md`: real random-instance population,
  a `DomainContract`, leak-audited structural predictors, held-out generator
  families, the discovery loop + `assess_outcome` gate, a pre-registered
  decision rule, and a stop rule.
- Inspect `git status`, the current diff, and recent history first. Preserve
  unrelated user changes and never reset or commit unless explicitly asked.
- Core RDE must not import domain plugins; adapters register via `rde.domains`.
- Treat backend, dtype, shape, memory, and numerical semantics as contracts.
  Add a regression test with each behavior or performance change.
- Mask non-finite data, guard denominators, reject constant inputs, and keep
  undefined statistics as `NaN`.
- Test real CLI/parser boundaries and report/manifest wiring, not only helpers.
- Do not turn finite-size experiments into universal claims.
- Any non-trivial RDE run must show live, real progress (work counter + elapsed
  + ETA) and persist durable logs. `NullProgress()` is the explicit silence
  opt-out.
